R rounds. But I need to be more careful here—the fractional sumcheck runs once per segment, and with 2 segments and around 18 GKR rounds per segment, I'm looking at roughly 36 total GKR rounds. The actual number of sumcheck rounds depends on the GKR tree depths for each segment, which are determined by the number of interactions across the 623 AIRs, and those depths could vary between segments.\n\nThe nsys profiling data shows 141 instances of compute_round_and_revert, which is puzzling. If this kernel runs once per GKR round per segment, that would mean 141 total GKR rounds across both segments—roughly 70 per segment. That's significantly higher than my estimate of 34 rounds (17 per segment for a tree of 2^18 leaves). This suggests there might be multiple independent GKR executions per segment, possibly one for each interaction type, so I need to dig into the logup_zerocheck code to understand how many times the GKR is actually invoked.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1466,"cache_read_input_tokens":107133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1466},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"b3ad7cca-1e7f-4d27-b2a4-fcc19625f030"}
