ark, not just app proof. I can't easily separate them using kernel counts alone. Instead, I should rely on the wall-clock timing from spec.py: app proof LogUp GKR takes 522ms at APC 300, leaf recursion takes 472ms, and inner recursion takes 248ms. The fractional sumcheck within the app proof GKR is roughly 522ms minus the GKR input evaluation time, which from earlier measurements runs around 300–320ms.\n\nBut I'm getting confused by the different reports—some show LogUp GKR at 526ms, others mention GKR input eval dropping from 532ms to 318ms. I need to clarify whether \"LogUp GKR\" in spec.py refers to the entire operation (input eval plus fractional sumcheck) or just one component.\n\nLet me check the NVTX ranges in the nsys trace database to see how the timing spans are actually structured.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":894,"cache_read_input_tokens":115275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":894},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"aec38d4c-e5d2-4c93-aba9-a1e18022cddb"}
