{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AYbSPjiSq1CeKxYTE7vFcY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqkMAvY2BYyp73qfwABGBH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Tile-Level GKR Input Multi-Stream Distribution\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams.\n\nCurrently, one kernel launch per AIR processes ALL tiles (up to 256 tiles for height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) in an internal loop. This means one thread's stream is occupied for ~30-40ms per large AIR while other streams sit idle. By splitting these into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles each and distributing across threads, we enable 2x effective GPU concurrency for these bandwidth-bound kernels.\n\nExpected savings: 40-80ms on GKR input eval at APC 300 (primarily segment 0), translating to ~40-80ms improvement on STARK excl trace.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry point\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215` — `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\n### Work item construction (lines 232-250)\nBuilds one `GkrInputWorkItem` per AIR. Each work item holds references to `air_ctx`, `pk_air`, `l_skip`, `d_challenges`, and `leaves_ptr` (output destination).\n\n### Sorting and pre-allocation (lines 252-321)\nWork items sorted by descending height. Max buffer sizes computed across all items. Per-thread `GkrThreadBuffers` pre-allocated (intermediates, public_values, partition_ptrs, tmp).\n\n### Thread dispatch (lines 328-349)\nItems chunked contiguously: `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`. Each thread gets a contiguous slice. Worker loop: `for w in chunk { process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?; }`\n\n### Per-AIR processing — `process_gkr_input_air()` (lines 112-209)\n1. Collects `partitioned_main` pointers, copies to device (line 156)\n2. Copies `public_values` to device if present (line 142)\n3. Computes `num_rows_per_tile = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1)` (line 162)\n4. Launches ONE kernel call: `logup_gkr_input_eval(is_global, ..., height, num_rows_per_tile)` (line 174)\n5. Optional post-process for lifted traces (lines 189-208) — DOES NOT apply at APC 300 (l_skip=0)\n\n### CUDA kernel — `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` (gkr_input.cu:66-208)\nGrid: 256 blocks × 256 threads = TASK_SIZE threads. Internal tile loop:\n```c\nfor (uint32_t j = 0; j < num_rows_per_tile; j++) {\n    uint32_t row = task_offset + j * task_stride;\n    if (row < permutation_height) { /* evaluate DAG, write to d_fracs */ }\n}\n```\nEach tile processes TASK_SIZE rows. For height=2^24: 256 tiles, each taking ~0.15ms = ~38ms total per AIR on one stream.\n\n### CUDA launcher — `_logup_gkr_input_eval()` (gkr_input.cu:216-263)\nLaunches kernel with count=TASK_SIZE for GLOBAL, count=permutation_height for SCATTER.\n\n### Rust FFI — `logup_gkr_input_eval()` (cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:938-968)\nSafe wrapper around `_logup_gkr_input_eval` extern FFI.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add tile_offset parameter to CUDA kernel and launcher\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n\n**Kernel** (line 66): Add `tile_offset` parameter:\n```c\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL>\n__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,\n    /* ...existing params... */\n    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,\n    const uint32_t tile_offset      // NEW: starting tile index\n)\n```\n\n**Kernel tile loop** (line 94): Change from `j = 0` to `j = tile_offset`:\n```c\nfor (uint32_t j = tile_offset; j < tile_offset + num_rows_per_tile; j++) {\n```\n\n**Launcher** (line 216): Add `tile_offset` parameter, pass through to kernel:\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    /* ...existing params... */\n    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,\n    uint32_t tile_offset             // NEW\n)\n```\n\nPass `tile_offset` to both GLOBAL and SCATTER kernel templates.\n\n**Why**: Enables launching the kernel for a sub-range of tiles. When tile_offset=0 and num_rows_per_tile=total_tiles, behavior is identical to current code.\n\n### 2. Update Rust FFI binding\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\n**Extern declaration** (line 278): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `_logup_gkr_input_eval`.\n\n**Safe wrapper** (line 938): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `logup_gkr_input_eval`, pass through to FFI call.\n\n### 3. Define tile-level work item\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n\nAdd a new struct:\n```rust\nstruct GkrInputTileItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    air: &'a GkrInputWorkItem<'a, HS>,\n    tile_offset: u32,\n    tile_count: u32,\n}\n```\n\nThis references the original per-AIR work item and adds tile range information.\n\n**Why**: Separates per-AIR data (interaction rules, trace pointers) from per-tile scheduling. Multiple tile items can reference the same AIR.\n\n### 4. Split large AIRs into tile items\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\nAfter building and sorting `work_items` (line 252), add a new phase:\n\n```rust\n// Phase 1b: Split large GLOBAL AIRs into tile-level sub-tasks.\nconst MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM: u32 = 64; // ~4M rows per sub-task\n\nlet mut tile_items: Vec<GkrInputTileItem<HS>> = Vec::new();\nfor w in &work_items {\n    let height = w.air_ctx.height() as u32;\n    let total_tiles = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1);\n    let rules = &w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;\n    let is_global = rules.inner.buffer_size > 10;\n\n    if is_global && total_tiles > MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM && num_threads > 1 {\n        // Split into sub-tasks\n        let mut offset = 0u32;\n        while offset < total_tiles {\n            let count = (total_tiles - offset).min(MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM);\n            tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: offset, tile_count: count });\n            offset += count;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // Keep as single item (small AIRs, SCATTER AIRs, or single-threaded)\n        tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: 0, tile_count: total_tiles });\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSort tile_items by descending tile_count for load balancing (largest sub-tasks first, then round-robin distribution puts them on different threads).\n\n**Why**: Only large GLOBAL AIRs benefit from splitting. Small AIRs and SCATTER AIRs stay as single items to avoid unnecessary overhead. The threshold MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM=64 means sub-tasks process ~4M rows, large enough to amortize kernel launch overhead while small enough to enable 4-way concurrency for the largest AIRs (256 tiles → 4 sub-tasks).\n\n### 5. Adapt per-AIR processing for tile-level dispatch\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n\nCreate a new function `process_gkr_input_tile()`:\n```rust\nfn process_gkr_input_tile<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    item: &GkrInputTileItem<HS>,\n    buffers: &mut GkrThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n    let w = item.air;\n    // ... same setup as process_gkr_input_air (lines 116-171) ...\n    // BUT: pass tile_offset and tile_count to the kernel:\n    unsafe {\n        logup_gkr_input_eval(\n            is_global,\n            trace_output,\n            d_preprocessed,\n            &buffers.partition_ptrs,\n            d_public_values,\n            w.d_challenges,\n            &buffers.intermediates,\n            &rules.inner.d_rules,\n            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,\n            &rules.d_pair_idxs,\n            height as u32,\n            item.tile_count,       // was: num_rows_per_tile (total)\n            item.tile_offset,      // NEW\n        )?;\n    }\n    // Skip post-processing (lifted case) — only the LAST tile item\n    // for a given AIR should do post-processing if needed.\n    // At APC 300 with l_skip=0, this branch is never taken.\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\nThe per-AIR setup (partition_ptrs H2D, public_values H2D) happens each time a tile item is processed. For a split AIR on 4 threads, this setup is duplicated 4 times. The duplication is acceptable because the H2D copies are tiny (~64 bytes each) and the saved wall time from GPU concurrency far exceeds this overhead.\n\n### 6. Update thread dispatch to use tile items\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\nReplace the current dispatch (lines 328-349) with:\n\n```rust\nif num_threads <= 1 {\n    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n    for item in &tile_items {\n        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n    }\n} else {\n    // Round-robin distribution of tile items across threads\n    let mut per_thread: Vec<Vec<&GkrInputTileItem<HS>>> = (0..num_threads).map(|_| Vec::new()).collect();\n    for (i, item) in tile_items.iter().enumerate() {\n        per_thread[i % num_threads].push(item);\n    }\n\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n            .into_iter()\n            .zip(per_thread)\n            .map(|(mut bufs, items)| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n                    for item in items {\n                        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n                    }\n                    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n                    Ok(())\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        for handle in handles {\n            handle.join().unwrap()?;\n        }\n        Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n    })?;\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: Round-robin on the sorted tile_items (largest first) naturally distributes large sub-tasks across different threads, preventing any single thread from accumulating too much work.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each row is processed exactly once. With tile_offset and tile_count partitioning the [0, total_tiles) range, every row in [0, permutation_height) is covered exactly once across all sub-tasks.\n\n2. **Output writes**: `d_fracs[out_idx]` where `out_idx = (interaction_idx * permutation_height + row) * 2`. Each sub-task writes to non-overlapping row ranges. No data race.\n\n3. **Intermediates isolation**: Each thread uses its own pre-allocated intermediates buffer. Sub-tasks of the same AIR on different threads use different buffers. The intermediates are computed and consumed within each row (no cross-row dependency).\n\n4. **leaves buffer initialization**: `fill_zero()` + `current_stream_sync()` happens before any thread writes. Sub-tasks write to disjoint regions.\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has <100 AIRs → single-threaded path. Even in multi-threaded mode, small AIRs are not split (total_tiles <= MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM). Behavior is identical to current code.\n\n6. **Lifted trace correctness**: At APC 300 with l_skip=0, the lifted case (height != lifted_height) is never triggered. For safety, add a guard: if l_skip > 0 and height != lifted_height, don't split that AIR (keep as a single item). This ensures the post-processing step runs on a single thread with the complete output.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare STARK excl trace and LogUp GKR at APC 300 vs before (1302ms, 522ms)\n3. Compare per-segment GKR input eval timing from metrics (`prover.rap_constraints.logup_gkr.input_evals_time_ms`)\n4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression\n5. Profile with nsys to confirm increased concurrent kernel execution for large AIRs\n\n**Success criteria**: LogUp GKR at APC 300 improves by ≥30ms (from 522ms to ≤492ms). STARK excl trace ≥30ms improvement. No APC 0 regression.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- LogUp GKR improvement at APC 300 is <30ms\n- Any regression at APC 0 exceeding 15ms\n- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":224746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"output_tokens":45,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"8ec2a012-bff8-45de-92df-6734c1a8f8ff"}
