interaction_rules;\n    let is_global = rules.inner.buffer_size > 10;\n\n    if is_global && total_tiles > MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM && num_threads > 1 {\n        // Split into sub-tasks\n        let mut offset = 0u32;\n        while offset < total_tiles {\n            let count = (total_tiles - offset).min(MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM);\n            tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: offset, tile_count: count });\n            offset += count;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // Keep as single item (small AIRs, SCATTER AIRs, or single-threaded)\n        tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: 0, tile_count: total_tiles });\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSort tile_items by descending tile_count for load balancing (largest sub-tasks first, then round-robin distribution puts them on different threads).\n\n**Why**: Only large GLOBAL AIRs benefit from splitting. Small AIRs and SCATTER AIRs stay as single items to avoid unnecessary overhead. The threshold MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM=64 means sub-tasks process ~4M rows, large enough to amortize kernel launch overhead while small enough to enable 4-way concurrency for the largest AIRs (256 tiles → 4 sub-tasks).\n\n### 5. Adapt per-AIR processing for tile-level dispatch\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n\nCreate a new function `process_gkr_input_tile()`:\n```rust\nfn process_gkr_input_tile<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    item: &GkrInputTileItem<HS>,\n    buffers: &mut GkrThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n    let w = item.air;\n    // ... same setup as process_gkr_input_air (lines 116-171) ...\n    // BUT: pass tile_offset and tile_count to the kernel:\n    unsafe {\n        logup_gkr_input_eval(\n            is_global,\n            trace_output,\n            d_preprocessed,\n            &buffers.partition_ptrs,\n            d_public_values,\n            w.d_challenges,\n            &buffers.intermediates,\n            &rules.inner.d_rules,\n            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,\n            &rules.d_pair_idxs,\n            height as u32,\n            item.tile_count,       // was: num_rows_per_tile (total)\n            item.tile_offset,      // NEW\n        )?;\n    }\n    // Skip post-processing (lifted case) — only the LAST tile item\n    // for a given AIR should do post-processing if needed.\n    // At APC 300 with l_skip=0, this branch is never taken.\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\nThe per-AIR setup (partition_ptrs H2D, public_values H2D) happens each time a tile item is processed. For a split AIR on 4 threads, this setup is duplicated 4 times. The duplication is acceptable because the H2D copies are tiny (~64 bytes each) and the saved wall time from GPU concurrency far exceeds this overhead.\n\n### 6. Update thread dispatch to use tile items\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\nReplace the current dispatch (lines 328-349) with:\n\n```rust\nif num_threads <= 1 {\n    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n    for item in &tile_items {\n        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n    }\n} else {\n    // Round-robin distribution of tile items across threads\n    let mut per_thread: Vec<Vec<&GkrInputTileItem<HS>>> = (0..num_threads).map(|_| Vec::new()).collect();\n    for (i, item) in tile_items.iter().enumerate() {\n        per_thread[i % num_threads].push(item);\n    }\n\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n            .into_iter()\n            .zip(per_thread)\n            .map(|(mut bufs, items)| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n                    for item in items {\n                        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n                    }\n                    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n                    Ok(())\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        for handle in handles {\n            handle.join().unwrap()?;\n        }\n        Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n    })?;\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: Round-robin on the sorted tile_items (largest first) naturally distributes large sub-tasks across different threads, preventing any single thread from accumulating too much work.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each row is processed exactly once. With tile_offset and tile_count partitioning the [0, total_tiles) range, every row in [0, permutation_height) is covered exactly once across all sub-tasks.\n\n2. **Output writes**: `d_fracs[out_idx]` where `out_idx = (interaction_idx * permutation_height + row) * 2`. Each sub-task writes to non-overlapping row ranges. No data race.\n\n3. **Intermediates isolation**: Each thread uses its own pre-allocated intermediates buffer. Sub-tasks of the same AIR on different threads use different buffers. The intermediates are computed and consumed within each row (no cross-row dependency).\n\n4. **leaves buffer initialization**: `fill_zero()` + `current_stream_sync()` happens before any thread writes. Sub-tasks write to disjoint regions.\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has <100 AIRs → single-threaded path. Even in multi-threaded mode, small AIRs are not split (total_tiles <= MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM). Behavior is identical to current code.\n\n6. **Lifted trace correctness**: At APC 300 with l_skip=0, the lifted case (height != lifted_height) is never triggered. For safety, add a guard: if l_skip > 0 and height != lifted_height, don't split that AIR (keep as a single item). This ensures the post-processing step runs on a single thread with the complete output.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare STARK excl trace and LogUp GKR at APC 300 vs before (1302ms, 522ms)\n3. Compare per-segment GKR input eval timing from metrics (`prover.rap_constraints.logup_gkr.input_evals_time_ms`)\n4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression\n5. Profile with nsys to confirm increased concurrent kernel execution for large AIRs\n\n**Success criteria**: LogUp GKR at APC 300 improves by ≥30ms (from 522ms to ≤492ms). STARK excl trace ≥30ms improvement. No APC 0 regression.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- LogUp GKR improvement at APC 300 is <30ms\n- Any regression at APC 0 exceeding 15ms\n- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
