{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VVWeiWUfr6XfU7TyHLjGGF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream\n2\t\n3\tSplit large-AIR GKR input evaluation kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. Currently, each AIR is processed as a single unit on one thread's stream, meaning a large AIR with 256 tiles (height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) monopolizes one stream for ~30-40ms while other streams sit idle. By splitting large AIRs into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles and distributing them round-robin, multiple sub-tasks from the same AIR execute concurrently on different streams, improving GPU utilization from ~1x to ~2x effective parallelism for the bandwidth-bound kernels that dominate segment 0's 241ms wall time.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV8r9kKd5y1CDQdWewg3WA","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"a8995bcc-5b89-4444-bf1d-3694292a7d06","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:46:07.347Z"}
