{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RpRfsYP3k8nZvoPEDwp7qi","type":"tool_result","content":"autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md:5:Reduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md:7:Currently, one kernel launch per AIR processes ALL tiles (up to 256 tiles for height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) in an internal loop. This means one thread's stream is occupied for ~30-40ms per large AIR while other streams sit idle. By splitting these into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles each and distributing across threads, we enable 2x effective GPU concurrency for these bandwidth-bound kernels.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md:40:Each tile processes TASK_SIZE rows. For height=2^24: 256 tiles, each taking ~0.15ms = ~38ms total per AIR on one stream.\nautoopt-results/log.md:63:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-prealloc-round0-buffers/plan.md:7:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-prealloc-round0-buffers/plan.md:9:**Expected improvement**: Round 0 296ms → ~190-220ms (~75-106ms reduction, 25-36%). STARK excl trace ~70-100ms improvement (5-7%). Based on GKR prealloc precedent where seg1 (many small AIRs, allocation-dominated) improved 4.15x while seg0 (few large AIRs, kernel-dominated) improved 1.07x.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers/report.md:70:The dramatic per-segment asymmetry (seg1 improved 4.15x while seg0 only 1.07x) confirms the hypothesis: seg1 has many small AIRs where per-AIR allocation overhead dominated, while seg0 has fewer, larger AIRs where kernel execution time dominates.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers/report.md:85:The dramatic improvement in seg1 (4.15x for GKR input eval) vs modest improvement in seg0 (1.07x) confirms that allocation overhead was the primary bottleneck for segments with many small AIRs. For segments with fewer large AIRs, kernel execution time dominates and this optimization has diminishing returns.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers/report.md:91:- **Further improvements to GKR input eval**: seg0 at APC 300 still takes 256ms — this is dominated by kernel execution time for a few large AIRs, not allocation overhead. Improving seg0 would require kernel-level optimizations (e.g., fusing multiple small kernels, reducing per-kernel launch overhead).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md:7:LogUp GKR is 534ms (40.7% of STARK excl trace at APC 300). The GKR input eval sub-phase is ~302ms across 2 segments (~242ms seg0, ~62ms seg1). From nsight profiling: 486 GLOBAL-mode instances (464ms GPU time, median 760us) + 305 SCATTER-mode instances (63ms GPU time, median 111us). SCATTER AIRs each launch a tiny kernel with 4-16 blocks that underutilizes the 128 SMs.\nautoopt-results/task.md:3:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:8:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:12:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:14:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:493:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:494:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:500:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-203057-16-2-do.log:501:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260414-070315-22-2-do.log:15:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260414-070315-22-2-do.log:158:[Omitted long matching line]\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 20]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV8r9kKd5y1CDQdWewg3WA","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"674b55cb-d2c4-4f54-80dc-7c870342c8fe","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:46:40.852Z"}
