{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nzqn7gkFReHLGc98ZfHGRk","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-349-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-350-3. **APC 0 fallback**: Guard `work_items.len() >= 100` ensures APC 0 (99 AIRs) uses the unchanged single-threaded path. No SCATTER batching at APC 0.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-351-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md:352:4. **Lifting correctness**: Lifted SCATTER AIRs write to a shared `d_scatter_tmp` buffer (one at a time, sequentially on the background thread). Non-lifted SCATTER AIRs write directly to `leaves`. The tmp buffer is large enough for the biggest lifted SCATTER AIR.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-353-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-354-5. **Memory safety**: All descriptor pointers reference device data valid for the `log_gkr_input_evals` lifetime. SCATTER intermediates are local arrays (10 elements, no device buffer needed). The `d_scatter_tmp` buffer is allocated on the main thread and borrowed by the background thread within `thread::scope`.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval/plan.md-355-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV8r9kKd5y1CDQdWewg3WA","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"f83988ef-d4a3-4a40-82e1-037c4a2440b2","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:46:55.398Z"}
