{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018axYzmhFvz55jB3hZTuWnX","type":"tool_result","content":"autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md:7:Currently, one kernel launch per AIR processes ALL tiles (up to 256 tiles for height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) in an internal loop. This means one thread's stream is occupied for ~30-40ms per large AIR while other streams sit idle. By splitting these into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles each and distributing across threads, we enable 2x effective GPU concurrency for these bandwidth-bound kernels.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-tile-level-gkr-input-multistream/plan.md:40:Each tile processes TASK_SIZE rows. For height=2^24: 256 tiles, each taking ~0.15ms = ~38ms total per AIR on one stream.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates/report.md:30:| STARK excl trace | 2455ms | 1314ms | 1317ms | -1138ms, 1.86x lower | +3ms, within noise |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates/report.md:68:- The GKR input eval kernel is now memory-bandwidth-bound on main/preprocessed trace reads, not intermediates locality. Future improvements should target:\nautoopt-results/log.md:151:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/report.md:31:| Round 0 | 662ms | 242ms | 238ms | -424ms, 2.78x lower | -4ms, unchanged |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/report.md:33:| Openings | 413ms | 176ms | 175ms | -238ms, 2.36x lower | -1ms, unchanged |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/report.md:65:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers/report.md:7:The plan estimated ~47ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead from nsight profiling (37K/47K of 38ms allocs + 37K/49K of 21ms frees), expecting 40-55ms savings at APC 300.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/report.md:5:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/report.md:42:| Constraints | 1292ms | 1336ms | 1330ms | +38ms, 1.03x higher | -6ms, 1.00x |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/report.md:53:| Constraints | 1393ms | 1046ms | 1038ms | -355ms, 1.34x lower | -8ms, 1.01x lower |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md:5:Eliminate ~37,000 per-round `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls in MLE sumcheck fold rounds by replacing per-matrix individual allocations with a single bulk allocation per fold group per round. This targets the main-thread allocation overhead visible in nsight (47K mallocs for 38ms + 49K frees for 21ms = 59ms total), which is the primary cause of MLE Rounds reverse-scaling at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less total work).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md:50:Quantitative estimate from nsight: the fold accounts for ~(37K/47K) × 38ms allocs + ~(37K/49K) × 21ms frees ≈ 31ms + 16ms = **~47ms** of pure CUDA memory API overhead. Additional savings from reduced memory pool fragmentation bring the total to ~40–55ms.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload/plan.md:41:**Count**: Case A fires once per trace across all rounds (~310 per segment × 2 segments = ~620 calls). Case B fires for each trace where `round <= n_lift`, decreasing as rounds progress. Total across all rounds and segments: ~3000-4000 calls. At ~15-20μs per call including deallocation, this is ~45-80ms of overhead, of which ~30-40ms is on the critical path (allocation + copy; deallocation is deferred to function exit).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels/report.md:38:| SR MLE APC 0 | 144ms | 59ms | 38ms | -106ms, 3.79x lower | -21ms, 1.55x lower |\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/report.md:58:- **Memory bandwidth analysis**: Use nsys memory throughput metrics to determine whether GKR input eval is compute-bound or memory-bound. If memory-bound, SM-level concurrency improvements won't help.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/plan.md:53:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers/report.md:91:- **Further improvements to GKR input eval**: seg0 at APC 300 still takes 256ms — this is dominated by kernel execution time for a few large AIRs, not allocation overhead. Improving seg0 would require kernel-level optimizations (e.g., fusing multiple small kernels, reducing per-kernel launch overhead).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0/plan.md:156:- STARK excl trace: 2138ms → 2138ms (unchanged)\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 20]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV8r9kKd5y1CDQdWewg3WA","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"38d2bf46-9470-416a-b7d9-0d3ffdcca0ae","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:46:56.672Z"}
