{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DK7iT6WzKzmCgoQ4PNoNXr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JGjDMLMac7fUzKNXZDvMcs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers\n\nReplace per-round DeviceMatrix allocations in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) with pre-allocated contiguous ping-pong buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~1400 new DeviceMatrix objects (one per foldable trace matrix across mat_evals and sels) and frees the previous round's ~1400 matrices, totaling ~37K cudaMallocAsync + ~37K cudaFreeAsync calls across 24 MLE rounds at APC 300. By pre-allocating two contiguous buffers (one for even rounds, one for odd) and computing per-trace offsets by halving the previous round's layout, we eliminate all per-round allocation/deallocation overhead (~15-20ms) while preserving the existing batched fold kernel.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5344,"cache_read_input_tokens":243844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5344},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"da766501-5520-4fe8-8f12-b34ea5e26d33"}
