{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011EjpaSFzgFM8DRWJtfMmwL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Tile-Level GKR Input Multi-Stream Distribution\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"25f8a03f-de1f-4fe2-9fbe-daa6dd38bbbd","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:56:29.947Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Tile-Level GKR Input Multi-Stream Distribution\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams.","numLines":5,"startLine":1,"totalLines":255}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DL4ryTNYweyHrBHss6Rqm8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01828ppg8a9F9zCBbPdJSUsH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### MLE Rounds loop\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n```rust\nfor round in 1..=n_max {\n    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n}\n```\n\n### fold_mle_evals\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n\nContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n\nCalled twice per round:\n- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n\nPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\nPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\nAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n\n### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n\nReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n\n### into_column_openings\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n\nCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n```rust\n/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\nmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\nmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\nmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\nmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\nmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n/// Same for sels\nsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\nsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n\n```rust\n// Compute sizes and total cells\nlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len())\n    .collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\nlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\n// Allocate ping-pong buffers\nlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n\n// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.\n\n### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n\n```rust\nfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n\n        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n            .collect();\n        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| {\n                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n                ptr\n            })\n            .collect();\n        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n            .collect();\n        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n            .collect();\n        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n            .max()\n            .unwrap_or(0);\n\n        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n\n        unsafe {\n            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n        }\n\n        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n        out_off = 0;\n        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n        }\n        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n            unsafe {\n                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n            }\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += cells;\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    };\n\n    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n\n    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n\n    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n    }\n    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace reads of `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` with helper:\n\n```rust\nfn mat_view(&self, flat_idx: usize, mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)],\n            mat_offsets: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>) -> (*const EF, usize, usize) {\n    let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n    (unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) }, h, w)\n}\n```\n\nSimilarly for sels. The flat index is computed from `mat_per_trace_counts` prefix sums.\n\nKey call sites to update:\n- Line 1604: `mats[0].buffer().as_ptr()` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).0`\n- Line 1605: `air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width())` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).2`\n- Line 1614: `mats[first_main_idx..].iter().map(...)` → iterate over flat indices\n- Line 1631: `sels.buffer().as_ptr()` → `sel_view(trace_idx, ...).0`\n- Line 1676: column pointer collection in Case B\n\n### 5. Update into_column_openings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:\n```rust\nfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],\n    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n        for _ in 0..count {\n            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };\n            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };\n            trace_openings.push(data);\n            flat_idx += 1;\n        }\n        result.push(trace_openings);\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self).\n\n### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n```rust\nif self.save_memory {\n    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n}\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n\n2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n\n3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: O(num_height1_matrices × 1 element) per round — negligible.\n\n4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n\n6. **into_column_openings**: Uses from_raw_parts for non-owning D2H. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call (it's part of self which is consumed by into_column_openings).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- APC 0 regression >10ms\n- Correctness failure\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":257260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"cbf01d04-55ee-4a43-a87d-7a1227ddaa2a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01828ppg8a9F9zCBbPdJSUsH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"4d698eb6-e991-49b2-bdac-856b114306e8","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:57:38.122Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### MLE Rounds loop\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n```rust\nfor round in 1..=n_max {\n    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n}\n```\n\n### fold_mle_evals\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n\nContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n\nCalled twice per round:\n- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n\nPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\nPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\nAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n\n### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n\nReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n\n### into_column_openings\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n\nCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n```rust\n/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\nmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\nmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\nmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\nmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\nmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n/// Same for sels\nsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\nsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n\n```rust\n// Compute sizes and total cells\nlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len())\n    .collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\nlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\n// Allocate ping-pong buffers\nlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n\n// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.\n\n### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n\n```rust\nfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n\n        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n            .collect();\n        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| {\n                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n                ptr\n            })\n            .collect();\n        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n            .collect();\n        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n            .collect();\n        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n            .max()\n            .unwrap_or(0);\n\n        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n\n        unsafe {\n            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n        }\n\n        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n        out_off = 0;\n        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n        }\n        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n            unsafe {\n                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n            }\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += cells;\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    };\n\n    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n\n    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n\n    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n    }\n    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace reads of `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` with helper:\n\n```rust\nfn mat_view(&self, flat_idx: usize, mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)],\n            mat_offsets: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>) -> (*const EF, usize, usize) {\n    let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n    (unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) }, h, w)\n}\n```\n\nSimilarly for sels. The flat index is computed from `mat_per_trace_counts` prefix sums.\n\nKey call sites to update:\n- Line 1604: `mats[0].buffer().as_ptr()` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).0`\n- Line 1605: `air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width())` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).2`\n- Line 1614: `mats[first_main_idx..].iter().map(...)` → iterate over flat indices\n- Line 1631: `sels.buffer().as_ptr()` → `sel_view(trace_idx, ...).0`\n- Line 1676: column pointer collection in Case B\n\n### 5. Update into_column_openings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:\n```rust\nfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],\n    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n        for _ in 0..count {\n            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };\n            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };\n            trace_openings.push(data);\n            flat_idx += 1;\n        }\n        result.push(trace_openings);\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self).\n\n### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n```rust\nif self.save_memory {\n    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n}\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n\n2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n\n3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: O(num_height1_matrices × 1 element) per round — negligible.\n\n4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n\n6. **into_column_openings**: Uses from_raw_parts for non-owning D2H. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call (it's part of self which is consumed by into_column_openings).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- APC 0 regression >10ms\n- Correctness failure\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":254,"newStart":1,"newLines":307,"lines":["-# Plan: Tile-Level GKR Input Multi-Stream Distribution","+# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers"," "," ## Goal"," ","-Reduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams.","+Eliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt."," ","-Currently, one kernel launch per AIR processes ALL tiles (up to 256 tiles for height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) in an internal loop. This means one thread's stream is occupied for ~30-40ms per large AIR while other streams sit idle. By splitting these into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles each and distributing across threads, we enable 2x effective GPU concurrency for these bandwidth-bound kernels.","-","-Expected savings: 40-80ms on GKR input eval at APC 300 (primarily segment 0), translating to ~40-80ms improvement on STARK excl trace.","-"," ## Current Code Path"," ","-### Entry point","-`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215` — `log_gkr_input_evals()`","+### MLE Rounds loop","+`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`","+```rust","+for round in 1..=n_max {","+    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;","+    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...","+    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;","+}","+```"," ","-### Work item construction (lines 232-250)","-Builds one `GkrInputWorkItem` per AIR. Each work item holds references to `air_ctx`, `pk_air`, `l_skip`, `d_challenges`, and `leaves_ptr` (output destination).","+### fold_mle_evals","+`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`"," ","-### Sorting and pre-allocation (lines 252-321)","-Work items sorted by descending height. Max buffer sizes computed across all items. Per-thread `GkrThreadBuffers` pre-allocated (intermediates, public_values, partition_ptrs, tmp).","+Contains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):","+1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)","+2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`","+3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)","+4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)","+5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)","+6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each"," ","-### Thread dispatch (lines 328-349)","-Items chunked contiguously: `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`. Each thread gets a contiguous slice. Worker loop: `for w in chunk { process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?; }`","+Called twice per round:","+- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300","+- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices"," ","-### Per-AIR processing — `process_gkr_input_air()` (lines 112-209)","-1. Collects `partitioned_main` pointers, copies to device (line 156)","-2. Copies `public_values` to device if present (line 142)","-3. Computes `num_rows_per_tile = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1)` (line 162)","-4. Launches ONE kernel call: `logup_gkr_input_eval(is_global, ..., height, num_rows_per_tile)` (line 174)","-5. Optional post-process for lifted traces (lines 189-208) — DOES NOT apply at APC 300 (l_skip=0)","+Per round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.","+Per benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).","+At 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead)."," ","-### CUDA kernel — `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` (gkr_input.cu:66-208)","-Grid: 256 blocks × 256 threads = TASK_SIZE threads. Internal tile loop:","-```c","-for (uint32_t j = 0; j < num_rows_per_tile; j++) {","-    uint32_t row = task_offset + j * task_stride;","-    if (row < permutation_height) { /* evaluate DAG, write to d_fracs */ }","-}","-```","-Each tile processes TASK_SIZE rows. For height=2^24: 256 tiles, each taking ~0.15ms = ~38ms total per AIR on one stream.","+### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval","+`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`"," ","-### CUDA launcher — `_logup_gkr_input_eval()` (gkr_input.cu:216-263)","-Launches kernel with count=TASK_SIZE for GLOBAL, count=permutation_height for SCATTER.","+Reads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced."," ","-### Rust FFI — `logup_gkr_input_eval()` (cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:938-968)","-Safe wrapper around `_logup_gkr_input_eval` extern FFI.","+### into_column_openings","+`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`"," ","+Calls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.","+"," ## Changes"," ","-### 1. Add tile_offset parameter to CUDA kernel and launcher","+### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-**Kernel** (line 66): Add `tile_offset` parameter:","-```c","-template <bool GLOBAL>","-__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(","-    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,","-    /* ...existing params... */","-    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,","-    const uint32_t tile_offset      // NEW: starting tile index","-)","+Add fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:","+```rust","+/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)","+mat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)","+mat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)","+mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,","+/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer","+mat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,","+/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)","+mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,","+/// Same for sels","+sel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+sel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,","+sel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,"," ```"," ","-**Kernel tile loop** (line 94): Change from `j = 0` to `j = tile_offset`:","-```c","-for (uint32_t j = tile_offset; j < tile_offset + num_rows_per_tile; j++) {","-```","+### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop"," ","-**Launcher** (line 216): Add `tile_offset` parameter, pass through to kernel:","-```c","-extern \"C\" int _logup_gkr_input_eval(","-    /* ...existing params... */","-    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,","-    uint32_t tile_offset             // NEW","-)","-```","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-Pass `tile_offset` to both GLOBAL and SCATTER kernel templates.","+After `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:"," ","-**Why**: Enables launching the kernel for a sub-range of tiles. When tile_offset=0 and num_rows_per_tile=total_tiles, behavior is identical to current code.","+```rust","+// Compute sizes and total cells","+let mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()","+    .flatten()","+    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))","+    .collect();","+let mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()","+    .map(|v| v.len())","+    .collect();","+let mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();"," ","-### 2. Update Rust FFI binding","+let sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()","+    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))","+    .collect();","+let sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`","+// Allocate ping-pong buffers","+let mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);","+let mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);","+let mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);","+let mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);"," ","-**Extern declaration** (line 278): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `_logup_gkr_input_eval`.","+// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies","+let mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());","+let mut off = 0usize;","+for m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {","+    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }","+    mat_offsets.push(off);","+    off += m.buffer().len();","+}","+// Same for sels into sel_buf_a","+let mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());","+off = 0;","+for m in &self.sels_per_trace {","+    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }","+    sel_offsets.push(off);","+    off += m.buffer().len();","+}"," ","-**Safe wrapper** (line 938): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `logup_gkr_input_eval`, pass through to FFI call.","+// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors","+drop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));","+drop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));","+```"," ","-### 3. Define tile-level work item","+**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding."," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`","+### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation"," ","-Add a new struct:","-```rust","-struct GkrInputTileItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {","-    air: &'a GkrInputWorkItem<'a, HS>,","-    tile_offset: u32,","-    tile_count: u32,","-}","-```","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-This references the original per-AIR work item and adds tile range information.","+New method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:"," ","-**Why**: Separates per-AIR data (interaction rules, trace pointers) from per-tile scheduling. Multiple tile items can reference the same AIR.","+```rust","+fn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(","+    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,","+    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],","+    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],","+    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {","+    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)","+    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],","+                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {","+        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);","+        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }"," ","-### 4. Split large AIRs into tile items","+        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)","+            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })","+            .collect();","+        let mut out_off = 0usize;","+        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)","+            .map(|i| {","+                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };","+                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;","+                ptr","+            })","+            .collect();","+        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)","+            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)","+            .collect();","+        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)","+            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)","+            .collect();","+        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)","+            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)","+            .max()","+            .unwrap_or(0);"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`","+        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;","+        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;","+        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;","+        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;"," ","-After building and sorting `work_items` (line 252), add a new phase:","+        unsafe {","+            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,","+                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;","+        }"," ","-```rust","-// Phase 1b: Split large GLOBAL AIRs into tile-level sub-tasks.","-const MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM: u32 = 64; // ~4M rows per sub-task","+        // Update sizes and offsets for next round","+        out_off = 0;","+        for i in 0..num_foldable {","+            sizes[i].0 /= 2;","+            offsets[i] = out_off;","+            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;","+        }","+        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout","+        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {","+            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;","+            unsafe {","+                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),","+                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);","+            }","+            offsets[i] = out_off;","+            out_off += cells;","+        }","+        Ok(())","+    };"," ","-let mut tile_items: Vec<GkrInputTileItem<HS>> = Vec::new();","-for w in &work_items {","-    let height = w.air_ctx.height() as u32;","-    let total_tiles = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1);","-    let rules = &w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;","-    let is_global = rules.inner.buffer_size > 10;","+    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;","+    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);"," ","-    if is_global && total_tiles > MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM && num_threads > 1 {","-        // Split into sub-tasks","-        let mut offset = 0u32;","-        while offset < total_tiles {","-            let count = (total_tiles - offset).min(MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM);","-            tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: offset, tile_count: count });","-            offset += count;","-        }","-    } else {","-        // Keep as single item (small AIRs, SCATTER AIRs, or single-threaded)","-        tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: 0, tile_count: total_tiles });","+    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;","+    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);","+","+    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)","+    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {","+        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }","     }","+    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];","+    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);","+    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);","+    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);","+    Ok(())"," }"," ```"," ","-Sort tile_items by descending tile_count for load balancing (largest sub-tasks first, then round-robin distribution puts them on different threads).","+### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views"," ","-**Why**: Only large GLOBAL AIRs benefit from splitting. Small AIRs and SCATTER AIRs stay as single items to avoid unnecessary overhead. The threshold MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM=64 means sub-tasks process ~4M rows, large enough to amortize kernel launch overhead while small enough to enable 4-way concurrency for the largest AIRs (256 tiles → 4 sub-tasks).","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-### 5. Adapt per-AIR processing for tile-level dispatch","+Replace reads of `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` with helper:"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`","-","-Create a new function `process_gkr_input_tile()`:"," ```rust","-fn process_gkr_input_tile<HS: GpuHashScheme>(","-    item: &GkrInputTileItem<HS>,","-    buffers: &mut GkrThreadBuffers,","-) -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {","-    let w = item.air;","-    // ... same setup as process_gkr_input_air (lines 116-171) ...","-    // BUT: pass tile_offset and tile_count to the kernel:","-    unsafe {","-        logup_gkr_input_eval(","-            is_global,","-            trace_output,","-            d_preprocessed,","-            &buffers.partition_ptrs,","-            d_public_values,","-            w.d_challenges,","-            &buffers.intermediates,","-            &rules.inner.d_rules,","-            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,","-            &rules.d_pair_idxs,","-            height as u32,","-            item.tile_count,       // was: num_rows_per_tile (total)","-            item.tile_offset,      // NEW","-        )?;","-    }","-    // Skip post-processing (lifted case) — only the LAST tile item","-    // for a given AIR should do post-processing if needed.","-    // At APC 300 with l_skip=0, this branch is never taken.","-    Ok(())","+fn mat_view(&self, flat_idx: usize, mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)],","+            mat_offsets: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>) -> (*const EF, usize, usize) {","+    let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];","+    (unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) }, h, w)"," }"," ```"," ","-The per-AIR setup (partition_ptrs H2D, public_values H2D) happens each time a tile item is processed. For a split AIR on 4 threads, this setup is duplicated 4 times. The duplication is acceptable because the H2D copies are tiny (~64 bytes each) and the saved wall time from GPU concurrency far exceeds this overhead.","+Similarly for sels. The flat index is computed from `mat_per_trace_counts` prefix sums."," ","-### 6. Update thread dispatch to use tile items","+Key call sites to update:","+- Line 1604: `mats[0].buffer().as_ptr()` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).0`","+- Line 1605: `air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width())` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).2`","+- Line 1614: `mats[first_main_idx..].iter().map(...)` → iterate over flat indices","+- Line 1631: `sels.buffer().as_ptr()` → `sel_view(trace_idx, ...).0`","+- Line 1676: column pointer collection in Case B"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`","+### 5. Update into_column_openings"," ","-Replace the current dispatch (lines 328-349) with:","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","+Replace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:"," ```rust","-if num_threads <= 1 {","-    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();","-    for item in &tile_items {","-        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;","-    }","-} else {","-    // Round-robin distribution of tile items across threads","-    let mut per_thread: Vec<Vec<&GkrInputTileItem<HS>>> = (0..num_threads).map(|_| Vec::new()).collect();","-    for (i, item) in tile_items.iter().enumerate() {","-        per_thread[i % num_threads].push(item);","-    }","-","-    std::thread::scope(|s| {","-        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers","-            .into_iter()","-            .zip(per_thread)","-            .map(|(mut bufs, items)| {","-                s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {","-                    for item in items {","-                        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;","-                    }","-                    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;","-                    Ok(())","-                })","-            })","-            .collect();","-        for handle in handles {","-            handle.join().unwrap()?;","+fn into_column_openings_pingpong(","+    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],","+    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {","+    let mut flat_idx = 0;","+    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());","+    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {","+        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);","+        for _ in 0..count {","+            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];","+            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };","+            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };","+            trace_openings.push(data);","+            flat_idx += 1;","         }","-        Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())","-    })?;","+        result.push(trace_openings);","+    }","+    Ok(result)"," }"," ```"," ","-**Why**: Round-robin on the sorted tile_items (largest first) naturally distributes large sub-tasks across different threads, preventing any single thread from accumulating too much work.","+Note: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self)."," ","+### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path","+","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`","+","+Lines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:","+```rust","+if self.save_memory {","+    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();","+    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution","+        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());","+}","+```","+"," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Correctness**: Each row is processed exactly once. With tile_offset and tile_count partitioning the [0, total_tiles) range, every row in [0, permutation_height) is covered exactly once across all sub-tasks.","+1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes."," ","-2. **Output writes**: `d_fracs[out_idx]` where `out_idx = (interaction_idx * permutation_height + row) * 2`. Each sub-task writes to non-overlapping row ranges. No data race.","+2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output."," ","-3. **Intermediates isolation**: Each thread uses its own pre-allocated intermediates buffer. Sub-tasks of the same AIR on different threads use different buffers. The intermediates are computed and consumed within each row (no cross-row dependency).","+3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: O(num_height1_matrices × 1 element) per round — negligible."," ","-4. **leaves buffer initialization**: `fill_zero()` + `current_stream_sync()` happens before any thread writes. Sub-tasks write to disjoint regions.","+4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB)."," ","-5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has <100 AIRs → single-threaded path. Even in multi-threaded mode, small AIRs are not split (total_tiles <= MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM). Behavior is identical to current code.","+5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive."," ","-6. **Lifted trace correctness**: At APC 300 with l_skip=0, the lifted case (height != lifted_height) is never triggered. For safety, add a guard: if l_skip > 0 and height != lifted_height, don't split that AIR (keep as a single item). This ensures the post-processing step runs on a single thread with the complete output.","+6. **into_column_openings**: Uses from_raw_parts for non-owning D2H. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call (it's part of self which is consumed by into_column_openings)."," "," ## Measurement Plan"," ","-1. Build and run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 300}","-2. Compare STARK excl trace and LogUp GKR at APC 300 vs before (1302ms, 522ms)","-3. Compare per-segment GKR input eval timing from metrics (`prover.rap_constraints.logup_gkr.input_evals_time_ms`)","-4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression","-5. Profile with nsys to confirm increased concurrent kernel execution for large AIRs","+1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}","+2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms","+3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms","+4. Verify APC 0 no regression","+5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)"," ","-**Success criteria**: LogUp GKR at APC 300 improves by ≥30ms (from 522ms to ≤492ms). STARK excl trace ≥30ms improvement. No APC 0 regression.","-"," ## Rollback Criteria"," ","-- LogUp GKR improvement at APC 300 is <30ms","-- Any regression at APC 0 exceeding 15ms","-- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)","+- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms","+- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms","+- APC 0 regression >10ms","+- Correctness failure"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Tile-Level GKR Input Multi-Stream Distribution\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce GKR input evaluation wall time at APC 300 by splitting large-AIR kernel launches into tile-level sub-tasks distributed across multiple CUDA streams. The primary target is segment 0, where input eval takes 241ms due to a few large AIRs (height=2^24) monopolizing single streams.\n\nCurrently, one kernel launch per AIR processes ALL tiles (up to 256 tiles for height=2^24, TASK_SIZE=65536) in an internal loop. This means one thread's stream is occupied for ~30-40ms per large AIR while other streams sit idle. By splitting these into sub-tasks of ≤64 tiles each and distributing across threads, we enable 2x effective GPU concurrency for these bandwidth-bound kernels.\n\nExpected savings: 40-80ms on GKR input eval at APC 300 (primarily segment 0), translating to ~40-80ms improvement on STARK excl trace.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry point\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215` — `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\n### Work item construction (lines 232-250)\nBuilds one `GkrInputWorkItem` per AIR. Each work item holds references to `air_ctx`, `pk_air`, `l_skip`, `d_challenges`, and `leaves_ptr` (output destination).\n\n### Sorting and pre-allocation (lines 252-321)\nWork items sorted by descending height. Max buffer sizes computed across all items. Per-thread `GkrThreadBuffers` pre-allocated (intermediates, public_values, partition_ptrs, tmp).\n\n### Thread dispatch (lines 328-349)\nItems chunked contiguously: `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`. Each thread gets a contiguous slice. Worker loop: `for w in chunk { process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?; }`\n\n### Per-AIR processing — `process_gkr_input_air()` (lines 112-209)\n1. Collects `partitioned_main` pointers, copies to device (line 156)\n2. Copies `public_values` to device if present (line 142)\n3. Computes `num_rows_per_tile = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1)` (line 162)\n4. Launches ONE kernel call: `logup_gkr_input_eval(is_global, ..., height, num_rows_per_tile)` (line 174)\n5. Optional post-process for lifted traces (lines 189-208) — DOES NOT apply at APC 300 (l_skip=0)\n\n### CUDA kernel — `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` (gkr_input.cu:66-208)\nGrid: 256 blocks × 256 threads = TASK_SIZE threads. Internal tile loop:\n```c\nfor (uint32_t j = 0; j < num_rows_per_tile; j++) {\n    uint32_t row = task_offset + j * task_stride;\n    if (row < permutation_height) { /* evaluate DAG, write to d_fracs */ }\n}\n```\nEach tile processes TASK_SIZE rows. For height=2^24: 256 tiles, each taking ~0.15ms = ~38ms total per AIR on one stream.\n\n### CUDA launcher — `_logup_gkr_input_eval()` (gkr_input.cu:216-263)\nLaunches kernel with count=TASK_SIZE for GLOBAL, count=permutation_height for SCATTER.\n\n### Rust FFI — `logup_gkr_input_eval()` (cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:938-968)\nSafe wrapper around `_logup_gkr_input_eval` extern FFI.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add tile_offset parameter to CUDA kernel and launcher\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n\n**Kernel** (line 66): Add `tile_offset` parameter:\n```c\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL>\n__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,\n    /* ...existing params... */\n    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,\n    const uint32_t tile_offset      // NEW: starting tile index\n)\n```\n\n**Kernel tile loop** (line 94): Change from `j = 0` to `j = tile_offset`:\n```c\nfor (uint32_t j = tile_offset; j < tile_offset + num_rows_per_tile; j++) {\n```\n\n**Launcher** (line 216): Add `tile_offset` parameter, pass through to kernel:\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    /* ...existing params... */\n    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,\n    uint32_t tile_offset             // NEW\n)\n```\n\nPass `tile_offset` to both GLOBAL and SCATTER kernel templates.\n\n**Why**: Enables launching the kernel for a sub-range of tiles. When tile_offset=0 and num_rows_per_tile=total_tiles, behavior is identical to current code.\n\n### 2. Update Rust FFI binding\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\n**Extern declaration** (line 278): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `_logup_gkr_input_eval`.\n\n**Safe wrapper** (line 938): Add `tile_offset: u32` parameter to `logup_gkr_input_eval`, pass through to FFI call.\n\n### 3. Define tile-level work item\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n\nAdd a new struct:\n```rust\nstruct GkrInputTileItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    air: &'a GkrInputWorkItem<'a, HS>,\n    tile_offset: u32,\n    tile_count: u32,\n}\n```\n\nThis references the original per-AIR work item and adds tile range information.\n\n**Why**: Separates per-AIR data (interaction rules, trace pointers) from per-tile scheduling. Multiple tile items can reference the same AIR.\n\n### 4. Split large AIRs into tile items\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\nAfter building and sorting `work_items` (line 252), add a new phase:\n\n```rust\n// Phase 1b: Split large GLOBAL AIRs into tile-level sub-tasks.\nconst MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM: u32 = 64; // ~4M rows per sub-task\n\nlet mut tile_items: Vec<GkrInputTileItem<HS>> = Vec::new();\nfor w in &work_items {\n    let height = w.air_ctx.height() as u32;\n    let total_tiles = height.div_ceil(TASK_SIZE).max(1);\n    let rules = &w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;\n    let is_global = rules.inner.buffer_size > 10;\n\n    if is_global && total_tiles > MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM && num_threads > 1 {\n        // Split into sub-tasks\n        let mut offset = 0u32;\n        while offset < total_tiles {\n            let count = (total_tiles - offset).min(MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM);\n            tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: offset, tile_count: count });\n            offset += count;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // Keep as single item (small AIRs, SCATTER AIRs, or single-threaded)\n        tile_items.push(GkrInputTileItem { air: w, tile_offset: 0, tile_count: total_tiles });\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSort tile_items by descending tile_count for load balancing (largest sub-tasks first, then round-robin distribution puts them on different threads).\n\n**Why**: Only large GLOBAL AIRs benefit from splitting. Small AIRs and SCATTER AIRs stay as single items to avoid unnecessary overhead. The threshold MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM=64 means sub-tasks process ~4M rows, large enough to amortize kernel launch overhead while small enough to enable 4-way concurrency for the largest AIRs (256 tiles → 4 sub-tasks).\n\n### 5. Adapt per-AIR processing for tile-level dispatch\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n\nCreate a new function `process_gkr_input_tile()`:\n```rust\nfn process_gkr_input_tile<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    item: &GkrInputTileItem<HS>,\n    buffers: &mut GkrThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n    let w = item.air;\n    // ... same setup as process_gkr_input_air (lines 116-171) ...\n    // BUT: pass tile_offset and tile_count to the kernel:\n    unsafe {\n        logup_gkr_input_eval(\n            is_global,\n            trace_output,\n            d_preprocessed,\n            &buffers.partition_ptrs,\n            d_public_values,\n            w.d_challenges,\n            &buffers.intermediates,\n            &rules.inner.d_rules,\n            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,\n            &rules.d_pair_idxs,\n            height as u32,\n            item.tile_count,       // was: num_rows_per_tile (total)\n            item.tile_offset,      // NEW\n        )?;\n    }\n    // Skip post-processing (lifted case) — only the LAST tile item\n    // for a given AIR should do post-processing if needed.\n    // At APC 300 with l_skip=0, this branch is never taken.\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\nThe per-AIR setup (partition_ptrs H2D, public_values H2D) happens each time a tile item is processed. For a split AIR on 4 threads, this setup is duplicated 4 times. The duplication is acceptable because the H2D copies are tiny (~64 bytes each) and the saved wall time from GPU concurrency far exceeds this overhead.\n\n### 6. Update thread dispatch to use tile items\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, in `log_gkr_input_evals()`\n\nReplace the current dispatch (lines 328-349) with:\n\n```rust\nif num_threads <= 1 {\n    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n    for item in &tile_items {\n        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n    }\n} else {\n    // Round-robin distribution of tile items across threads\n    let mut per_thread: Vec<Vec<&GkrInputTileItem<HS>>> = (0..num_threads).map(|_| Vec::new()).collect();\n    for (i, item) in tile_items.iter().enumerate() {\n        per_thread[i % num_threads].push(item);\n    }\n\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n            .into_iter()\n            .zip(per_thread)\n            .map(|(mut bufs, items)| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n                    for item in items {\n                        process_gkr_input_tile(item, &mut bufs)?;\n                    }\n                    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n                    Ok(())\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        for handle in handles {\n            handle.join().unwrap()?;\n        }\n        Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n    })?;\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: Round-robin on the sorted tile_items (largest first) naturally distributes large sub-tasks across different threads, preventing any single thread from accumulating too much work.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each row is processed exactly once. With tile_offset and tile_count partitioning the [0, total_tiles) range, every row in [0, permutation_height) is covered exactly once across all sub-tasks.\n\n2. **Output writes**: `d_fracs[out_idx]` where `out_idx = (interaction_idx * permutation_height + row) * 2`. Each sub-task writes to non-overlapping row ranges. No data race.\n\n3. **Intermediates isolation**: Each thread uses its own pre-allocated intermediates buffer. Sub-tasks of the same AIR on different threads use different buffers. The intermediates are computed and consumed within each row (no cross-row dependency).\n\n4. **leaves buffer initialization**: `fill_zero()` + `current_stream_sync()` happens before any thread writes. Sub-tasks write to disjoint regions.\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has <100 AIRs → single-threaded path. Even in multi-threaded mode, small AIRs are not split (total_tiles <= MAX_TILES_PER_ITEM). Behavior is identical to current code.\n\n6. **Lifted trace correctness**: At APC 300 with l_skip=0, the lifted case (height != lifted_height) is never triggered. For safety, add a guard: if l_skip > 0 and height != lifted_height, don't split that AIR (keep as a single item). This ensures the post-processing step runs on a single thread with the complete output.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare STARK excl trace and LogUp GKR at APC 300 vs before (1302ms, 522ms)\n3. Compare per-segment GKR input eval timing from metrics (`prover.rap_constraints.logup_gkr.input_evals_time_ms`)\n4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression\n5. Profile with nsys to confirm increased concurrent kernel execution for large AIRs\n\n**Success criteria**: LogUp GKR at APC 300 improves by ≥30ms (from 522ms to ≤492ms). STARK excl trace ≥30ms improvement. No APC 0 regression.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- LogUp GKR improvement at APC 300 is <30ms\n- Any regression at APC 0 exceeding 15ms\n- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n"}}
