{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133zzs16KWNoHPyfFMAUHDa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-round DeviceMatrix allocations in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) with pre-allocated contiguous ping-pong buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~1400 new DeviceMatrix objects (one per foldable trace matrix across mat_evals and sels) and frees the previous round's ~1400 matrices, totaling ~37K cudaMallocAsync + ~37K cudaFreeAsync calls across 24 MLE rounds at APC 300. By pre-allocating two contiguous buffers (one for even rounds, one for odd) and computing per-trace offsets by halving the previous round's layout, we eliminate all per-round allocation/deallocation overhead (~15-20ms) while preserving the existing batched fold kernel.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6PshVC9TeSKyqWgdvXfMu","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"78b774b9-292f-4b15-984a-1f38b568b7a5","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:57:57.981Z"}
