{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LFiufAB6pEwEVCMDukD537","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### MLE Rounds loop\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n11\t```rust\n12\tfor round in 1..=n_max {\n13\t    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n14\t    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n15\t    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n16\t}\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\t### fold_mle_evals\n20\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n21\t\n22\tContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n23\t1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n24\t2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n25\t3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n26\t4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n27\t5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n28\t6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n29\t\n30\tCalled twice per round:\n31\t- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n32\t- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n33\t\n34\tPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\n35\tPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\n36\tAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n37\t\n38\t### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n39\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n40\t\n41\tReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n42\t\n43\t### into_column_openings\n44\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n45\t\n46\tCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n47\t\n48\t## Changes\n49\t\n50\t### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n51\t\n52\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n53\t\n54\tAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n55\t```rust\n56\t/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\n57\tmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n58\t/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\n59\tmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n60\t/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\n61\tmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n62\t/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\n63\tmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n64\t/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\n65\tmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n66\t/// Same for sels\n67\tsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n68\tsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n69\tsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n70\tsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n74\t\n75\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n76\t\n77\tAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n78\t\n79\t```rust\n80\t// Compute sizes and total cells\n81\tlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n82\t    .flatten()\n83\t    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n84\t    .collect();\n85\tlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n86\t    .map(|v| v.len())\n87\t    .collect();\n88\tlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n89\t\n90\tlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n91\t    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n92\t    .collect();\n93\tlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n94\t\n95\t// Allocate ping-pong buffers\n96\tlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\n97\tlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\n98\tlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n99\tlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n100\t\n101\t// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\n102\tlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\n103\tlet mut off = 0usize;\n104\tfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n105\t    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n106\t    mat_offsets.push(off);\n107\t    off += m.buffer().len();\n108\t}\n109\t// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\n110\tlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\n111\toff = 0;\n112\tfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n113\t    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n114\t    sel_offsets.push(off);\n115\t    off += m.buffer().len();\n116\t}\n117\t\n118\t// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\n119\tdrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\n120\tdrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n121\t```\n122\t\n123\t**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.\n124\t\n125\t### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n126\t\n127\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n128\t\n129\tNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n130\t\n131\t```rust\n132\tfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n133\t    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n134\t    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n135\t    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n136\t    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n137\t    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n138\t) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n139\t    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n140\t    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n141\t                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n142\t        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n143\t        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n144\t\n145\t        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n146\t            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n147\t            .collect();\n148\t        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n149\t        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n150\t            .map(|i| {\n151\t                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n152\t                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n153\t                ptr\n154\t            })\n155\t            .collect();\n156\t        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n157\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n158\t            .collect();\n159\t        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n160\t            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n161\t            .collect();\n162\t        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n163\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n164\t            .max()\n165\t            .unwrap_or(0);\n166\t\n167\t        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n168\t        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n169\t        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n170\t        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n171\t\n172\t        unsafe {\n173\t            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n174\t                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n175\t        }\n176\t\n177\t        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n178\t        out_off = 0;\n179\t        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n180\t            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n181\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n182\t            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n183\t        }\n184\t        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n185\t        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n186\t            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n187\t            unsafe {\n188\t                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n189\t                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n190\t            }\n191\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n192\t            out_off += cells;\n193\t        }\n194\t        Ok(())\n195\t    };\n196\t\n197\t    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n198\t    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n199\t\n200\t    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n201\t    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n202\t\n203\t    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n204\t    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n205\t        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n206\t    }\n207\t    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n208\t    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n209\t    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n210\t    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n211\t    Ok(())\n212\t}\n213\t```\n214\t\n215\t### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n216\t\n217\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n218\t\n219\tReplace reads of `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` with helper:\n220\t\n221\t```rust\n222\tfn mat_view(&self, flat_idx: usize, mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)],\n223\t            mat_offsets: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>) -> (*const EF, usize, usize) {\n224\t    let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n225\t    (unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) }, h, w)\n226\t}\n227\t```\n228\t\n229\tSimilarly for sels. The flat index is computed from `mat_per_trace_counts` prefix sums.\n230\t\n231\tKey call sites to update:\n232\t- Line 1604: `mats[0].buffer().as_ptr()` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).0`\n233\t- Line 1605: `air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width())` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).2`\n234\t- Line 1614: `mats[first_main_idx..].iter().map(...)` → iterate over flat indices\n235\t- Line 1631: `sels.buffer().as_ptr()` → `sel_view(trace_idx, ...).0`\n236\t- Line 1676: column pointer collection in Case B\n237\t\n238\t### 5. Update into_column_openings\n239\t\n240\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n241\t\n242\tReplace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:\n243\t```rust\n244\tfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n245\t    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],\n246\t    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n247\t) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n248\t    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n249\t    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n250\t    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n251\t        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n252\t        for _ in 0..count {\n253\t            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n254\t            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };\n255\t            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };\n256\t            trace_openings.push(data);\n257\t            flat_idx += 1;\n258\t        }\n259\t        result.push(trace_openings);\n260\t    }\n261\t    Ok(result)\n262\t}\n263\t```\n264\t\n265\tNote: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self).\n266\t\n267\t### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n268\t\n269\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n270\t\n271\tLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n272\t```rust\n273\tif self.save_memory {\n274\t    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n275\t    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n276\t        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n277\t}\n278\t```\n279\t\n280\t## Invariants\n281\t\n282\t1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n283\t\n284\t2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n285\t\n286\t3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: O(num_height1_matrices × 1 element) per round — negligible.\n287\t\n288\t4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n289\t\n290\t5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n291\t\n292\t6. **into_column_openings**: Uses from_raw_parts for non-owning D2H. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call (it's part of self which is consumed by into_column_openings).\n293\t\n294\t## Measurement Plan\n295\t\n296\t1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n297\t2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n298\t3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n299\t4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n300\t5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n301\t\n302\t## Rollback Criteria\n303\t\n304\t- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n305\t- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n306\t- APC 0 regression >10ms\n307\t- Correctness failure\n308\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6PshVC9TeSKyqWgdvXfMu","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"2d05f25e-bad4-4bd2-961e-065368153fb8","timestamp":"2026-04-14T14:57:58.615Z"}
