{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149KXvNxz43frXwpbYqiBhe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### MLE Rounds loop\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"4cb6adab-9c4f-4b33-ab47-b9ce96158146","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:01:47.690Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### MLE Rounds loop\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`","numLines":10,"startLine":1,"totalLines":308}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BWeP5duJTqebP5rHQ6iHfS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U5wMASPMd829k7FeLFLXv8","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","old_string":"### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n\n```rust\n// Compute sizes and total cells\nlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len())\n    .collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\nlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\n// Allocate ping-pong buffers\nlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n\n// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.","new_string":"### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):\n\n```rust\n// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.\nstruct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }\n\nlet mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();\n// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array\nlet mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()\n    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\nlet sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\n// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,\n// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output.\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n```\n\n**Why (Improvement A from review)**: Skip the initial D2D packing entirely. Round 1 reads directly from the original `DeviceMatrix` objects, writes into buffer B. After round 1, drop the originals (freeing their memory) and allocate buffer A for round 2 output. This saves ~2-3ms of D2D packing cost.\n\n**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":266250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":563},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"40db88c1-c02c-4c03-ad34-004858d709e6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5wMASPMd829k7FeLFLXv8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"75ca4737-3b0b-44c7-a189-487c8e0960f1","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:02:10.661Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","oldString":"### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n\n```rust\n// Compute sizes and total cells\nlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len())\n    .collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\nlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\n// Allocate ping-pong buffers\nlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n\n// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.","newString":"### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):\n\n```rust\n// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.\nstruct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }\n\nlet mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();\n// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array\nlet mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()\n    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\nlet sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\n// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,\n// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output.\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n```\n\n**Why (Improvement A from review)**: Skip the initial D2D packing entirely. Round 1 reads directly from the original `DeviceMatrix` objects, writes into buffer B. After round 1, drop the originals (freeing their memory) and allocate buffer A for round 2 output. This saves ~2-3ms of D2D packing cost.\n\n**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.","originalFile":"# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### MLE Rounds loop\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n```rust\nfor round in 1..=n_max {\n    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n}\n```\n\n### fold_mle_evals\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n\nContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n\nCalled twice per round:\n- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n\nPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\nPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\nAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n\n### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n\nReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n\n### into_column_openings\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n\nCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n```rust\n/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\nmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\nmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\nmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\nmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\nmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n/// Same for sels\nsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\nsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:\n\n```rust\n// Compute sizes and total cells\nlet mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len())\n    .collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\nlet sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))\n    .collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();\n\n// Allocate ping-pong buffers\nlet mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n\n// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.\n\n### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n\n```rust\nfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n\n        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n            .collect();\n        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| {\n                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n                ptr\n            })\n            .collect();\n        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n            .collect();\n        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n            .collect();\n        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n            .max()\n            .unwrap_or(0);\n\n        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n\n        unsafe {\n            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n        }\n\n        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n        out_off = 0;\n        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n        }\n        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n            unsafe {\n                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n            }\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += cells;\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    };\n\n    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n\n    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n\n    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n    }\n    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace reads of `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` with helper:\n\n```rust\nfn mat_view(&self, flat_idx: usize, mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)],\n            mat_offsets: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>) -> (*const EF, usize, usize) {\n    let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n    (unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) }, h, w)\n}\n```\n\nSimilarly for sels. The flat index is computed from `mat_per_trace_counts` prefix sums.\n\nKey call sites to update:\n- Line 1604: `mats[0].buffer().as_ptr()` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).0`\n- Line 1605: `air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width())` → `mat_view(flat_base, ...).2`\n- Line 1614: `mats[first_main_idx..].iter().map(...)` → iterate over flat indices\n- Line 1631: `sels.buffer().as_ptr()` → `sel_view(trace_idx, ...).0`\n- Line 1676: column pointer collection in Case B\n\n### 5. Update into_column_openings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:\n```rust\nfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],\n    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n        for _ in 0..count {\n            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };\n            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };\n            trace_openings.push(data);\n            flat_idx += 1;\n        }\n        result.push(trace_openings);\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self).\n\n### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n```rust\nif self.save_memory {\n    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n}\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n\n2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n\n3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: O(num_height1_matrices × 1 element) per round — negligible.\n\n4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n\n6. **into_column_openings**: Uses from_raw_parts for non-owning D2H. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call (it's part of self which is consumed by into_column_openings).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- APC 0 regression >10ms\n- Correctness failure\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":74,"oldLines":54,"newStart":74,"newLines":37,"lines":[" "," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-After `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), pack current matrices into buffer A:","+After `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):"," "," ```rust","-// Compute sizes and total cells","-let mat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()","+// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.","+struct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }","+","+let mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()","     .flatten()","-    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))","+    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })","     .collect();"," let mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()","-    .map(|v| v.len())","-    .collect();","-let mat_total: usize = mat_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();","+    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();","+// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array","+let mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()","+    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();","+let mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();"," ","-let sel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()","-    .map(|m| (m.height(), m.width()))","-    .collect();","-let sel_total: usize = sel_fold_sizes.iter().map(|(h, w)| h * w).sum();","+let sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()","+    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();","+let sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();"," ","-// Allocate ping-pong buffers","-let mut mat_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);","+// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,","+// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output."," let mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);","-let mut sel_buf_a = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);"," let mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);","-","-// Pack mat_evals into buffer A via D2D copies","-let mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_fold_sizes.len());","-let mut off = 0usize;","-for m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {","-    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }","-    mat_offsets.push(off);","-    off += m.buffer().len();","-}","-// Same for sels into sel_buf_a","-let mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_fold_sizes.len());","-off = 0;","-for m in &self.sels_per_trace {","-    unsafe { cuda_memcpy_d2d(sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off), m.buffer().as_ptr(), m.buffer().len()); }","-    sel_offsets.push(off);","-    off += m.buffer().len();","-}","-","-// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors","-drop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));","-drop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));"," ```"," ","-**Why**: One-time D2D packing cost (~2-3ms) is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding.","+**Why (Improvement A from review)**: Skip the initial D2D packing entirely. Round 1 reads directly from the original `DeviceMatrix` objects, writes into buffer B. After round 1, drop the originals (freeing their memory) and allocate buffer A for round 2 output. This saves ~2-3ms of D2D packing cost."," ","+**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.","+"," ### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation"," "," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
