{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LAmA21LkSg6vePdaAv7isV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTLw6H4gTRQhXBVNdcwaPa","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","old_string":"### 5. Update into_column_openings to read from ping-pong buffer\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace `m.to_host()` with manual D2H from ping-pong buffer:\n```rust\nfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n    mat_sizes: &[(usize,usize)], mat_offsets: &[usize],\n    mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize], buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n        for _ in 0..count {\n            let (h, w) = mat_sizes[flat_idx];\n            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(mat_offsets[flat_idx]) };\n            let data = unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, h * w).to_host()? };\n            trace_openings.push(data);\n            flat_idx += 1;\n        }\n        result.push(trace_openings);\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates a non-owning view for D2H. Must ensure the ping-pong buffer outlives this call (it does, since into_column_openings consumes self).","new_string":"### 5. Update into_column_openings to read from ping-pong buffer\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nReplace `m.to_host()` with non-owning D2H from ping-pong buffer using `ManuallyDrop` to prevent double-free:\n\n```rust\nfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n    mat_slices: &[MatSlice], mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize],\n    buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n        for _ in 0..count {\n            let s = &mat_slices[flat_idx];\n            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) } as *mut EF;\n            // ManuallyDrop prevents Drop from calling d_free on this sub-buffer pointer.\n            let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n                unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, s.height * s.width) }\n            );\n            let data = view.to_host().map_err(LogupZerocheckError::MemCopy)?;\n            trace_openings.push(data);\n            flat_idx += 1;\n        }\n        result.push(trace_openings);\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\n**Why ManuallyDrop**: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates an owning buffer whose `Drop` calls `d_free`. Since the pointer is a sub-region of the ping-pong buffer (not a standalone allocation), `d_free` would corrupt the heap. `ManuallyDrop` suppresses the drop, and `to_host()` works on the non-owning reference for the D2H copy."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1425,"cache_read_input_tokens":268486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1425},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"887e574f-5166-4d61-81f2-19e77f337d5c"}
