{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013QFqgnz55bhzt2QKTb82mZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### MLE Rounds loop\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n11\t```rust\n12\tfor round in 1..=n_max {\n13\t    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n14\t    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n15\t    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n16\t}\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\t### fold_mle_evals\n20\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n21\t\n22\tContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n23\t1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n24\t2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n25\t3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n26\t4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n27\t5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n28\t6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n29\t\n30\tCalled twice per round:\n31\t- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n32\t- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n33\t\n34\tPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\n35\tPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\n36\tAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n37\t\n38\t### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n39\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n40\t\n41\tReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n42\t\n43\t### into_column_openings\n44\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n45\t\n46\tCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n47\t\n48\t## Changes\n49\t\n50\t### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n51\t\n52\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n53\t\n54\tAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n55\t```rust\n56\t/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\n57\tmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n58\t/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\n59\tmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n60\t/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\n61\tmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n62\t/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\n63\tmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n64\t/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\n65\tmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n66\t/// Same for sels\n67\tsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n68\tsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n69\tsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n70\tsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n74\t\n75\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n76\t\n77\tAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):\n78\t\n79\t```rust\n80\t// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.\n81\tstruct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }\n82\t\n83\tlet mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n84\t    .flatten()\n85\t    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })\n86\t    .collect();\n87\tlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n88\t    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();\n89\t// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array\n90\tlet mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()\n91\t    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();\n92\tlet mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n93\t\n94\tlet sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n95\t    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();\n96\tlet sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n97\t\n98\t// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,\n99\t// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output.\n100\tlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\n101\tlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t**Why (Improvement A from review)**: Skip the initial D2D packing entirely. Round 1 reads directly from the original `DeviceMatrix` objects, writes into buffer B. After round 1, drop the originals (freeing their memory) and allocate buffer A for round 2 output. This saves ~2-3ms of D2D packing cost.\n105\t\n106\t**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.\n107\t\n108\t### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n109\t\n110\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n111\t\n112\tNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n113\t\n114\t```rust\n115\tfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n116\t    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n117\t    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n118\t    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n119\t    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n120\t    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n121\t) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n122\t    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n123\t    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n124\t                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n125\t        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n126\t        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n127\t\n128\t        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n129\t            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n130\t            .collect();\n131\t        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n132\t        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n133\t            .map(|i| {\n134\t                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n135\t                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n136\t                ptr\n137\t            })\n138\t            .collect();\n139\t        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n140\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n141\t            .collect();\n142\t        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n143\t            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n144\t            .collect();\n145\t        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n146\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n147\t            .max()\n148\t            .unwrap_or(0);\n149\t\n150\t        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n151\t        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n152\t        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n153\t        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n154\t\n155\t        unsafe {\n156\t            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n157\t                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n158\t        }\n159\t\n160\t        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n161\t        out_off = 0;\n162\t        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n163\t            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n164\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n165\t            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n166\t        }\n167\t        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n168\t        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n169\t            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n170\t            unsafe {\n171\t                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n172\t                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n173\t            }\n174\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n175\t            out_off += cells;\n176\t        }\n177\t        Ok(())\n178\t    };\n179\t\n180\t    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n181\t    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n182\t\n183\t    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n184\t    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n185\t\n186\t    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n187\t    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n188\t        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n189\t    }\n190\t    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n191\t    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n192\t    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n193\t    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n194\t    Ok(())\n195\t}\n196\t```\n197\t\n198\t### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n199\t\n200\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n201\t\n202\tUse `MatSlice` and prefix sums to index into the ping-pong buffer. For each `trace_idx`, the flat range of matrices is `mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx]..mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx] + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx]`.\n203\t\n204\tAll call sites that access `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` or `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` need updating:\n205\t\n206\t**Case A.1 (late eval, lines 1601-1638)**: Accesses `mats[0]` for preprocessed and `mats[first_main_idx..]` for mains:\n207\t```rust\n208\tlet flat_base = mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx];\n209\t// Preprocessed (mat index 0 if has_preprocessed)\n210\tlet prep_ptr = if has_preprocessed {\n211\t    let s = &mat_slices[flat_base];\n212\t    MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n213\t} else { ... };\n214\t// Mains (indices first_main_idx..)\n215\tlet main_ptrs: Vec<_> = (flat_base + first_main_idx..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx])\n216\t    .map(|i| {\n217\t        let s = &mat_slices[i];\n218\t        MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n219\t    }).collect();\n220\t```\n221\t\n222\t**Case B (early eval, lines 1649-1685)**: Column pointer collection iterates columns:\n223\t```rust\n224\t// For sels:\n225\tlet sel = &sel_slices[trace_idx];\n226\tlet sel_ptr = unsafe { sel_buf.as_ptr().add(sel.offset) };\n227\tfor col in 0..sel.width {\n228\t    all_columns.push(unsafe { sel_ptr.add(col * sel.height) });  // column-major stride\n229\t}\n230\t// For each mat in trace:\n231\tfor i in flat_base..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx] {\n232\t    let s = &mat_slices[i];\n233\t    let mat_ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) };\n234\t    for col in 0..s.width {\n235\t        all_columns.push(unsafe { mat_ptr.add(col * s.height) });\n236\t    }\n237\t}\n238\t```\n239\t\n240\t**Key invariant**: Within each matrix's region in the ping-pong buffer, the column-major layout is preserved exactly (columns spaced by `height` elements) because the D2D/fold copies raw bytes in the same layout.\n241\t\n242\t**Phase 3 width accesses (lines 1749-1767)**: Replace `mats[0].width()` with `mat_slices[flat_base].width` and iteration over `mats[first_main_idx..]` with flat-index iteration using `mat_slices[flat_base + first_main_idx..].iter().map(|s| s.width)`.\n243\t\n244\t### 5. Update into_column_openings\n245\t\n246\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n247\t\n248\tReplace `m.to_host()` with non-owning D2H from ping-pong buffer using `ManuallyDrop` to prevent double-free:\n249\t\n250\t```rust\n251\tfn into_column_openings_pingpong(\n252\t    mat_slices: &[MatSlice], mat_per_trace_counts: &[usize],\n253\t    buf: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n254\t) -> Result<Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n255\t    let mut flat_idx = 0;\n256\t    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(mat_per_trace_counts.len());\n257\t    for &count in mat_per_trace_counts {\n258\t        let mut trace_openings = Vec::with_capacity(count);\n259\t        for _ in 0..count {\n260\t            let s = &mat_slices[flat_idx];\n261\t            let ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) } as *mut EF;\n262\t            // ManuallyDrop prevents Drop from calling d_free on this sub-buffer pointer.\n263\t            let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n264\t                unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, s.height * s.width) }\n265\t            );\n266\t            let data = view.to_host().map_err(LogupZerocheckError::MemCopy)?;\n267\t            trace_openings.push(data);\n268\t            flat_idx += 1;\n269\t        }\n270\t        result.push(trace_openings);\n271\t    }\n272\t    Ok(result)\n273\t}\n274\t```\n275\t\n276\t**Why ManuallyDrop**: `DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts` creates an owning buffer whose `Drop` calls `d_free`. Since the pointer is a sub-region of the ping-pong buffer (not a standalone allocation), `d_free` would corrupt the heap. `ManuallyDrop` suppresses the drop while `to_host()` still performs the D2H copy correctly.\n277\t\n278\t### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n279\t\n280\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n281\t\n282\tLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n283\t```rust\n284\tif self.save_memory {\n285\t    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n286\t    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n287\t        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n288\t}\n289\t```\n290\t\n291\t## Invariants\n292\t\n293\t1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n294\t\n295\t2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n296\t\n297\t3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: sum of (width) elements for all height-1 matrices. Even with 1400 matrices of average width 50, total copy is ~70K elements × 16 bytes = 560KB — well within a single async D2D latency (~0.1ms).\n298\t\n299\t4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n300\t\n301\t5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n302\t\n303\t6. **into_column_openings**: Uses `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer>` for non-owning D2H reads. The ping-pong buffer is alive during this call. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the double-free that would occur if the sub-buffer's `Drop` called `d_free` on a mid-allocation pointer.\n304\t\n305\t## Measurement Plan\n306\t\n307\t1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n308\t2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n309\t3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n310\t4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n311\t5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n312\t\n313\t## Rollback Criteria\n314\t\n315\t- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n316\t- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n317\t- APC 0 regression >10ms\n318\t- Correctness failure\n319\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRM88RjihKG73ZqoC41xCi","session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"2eadcb2a-9239-43ba-9ee9-44534be1fa29","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:03:33.932Z"}
