{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Pms5zypBQwmUr48bxZ7DUg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NfsD1xfGkGnre83PffMoZJ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","old_string":"**Why (Improvement A from review)**: Skip the initial D2D packing entirely. Round 1 reads directly from the original `DeviceMatrix` objects, writes into buffer B. After round 1, drop the originals (freeing their memory) and allocate buffer A for round 2 output. This saves ~2-3ms of D2D packing cost.\n\n**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.","new_string":"**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.\n\nPack mat_evals and sels into their respective buffer A via D2D copies:\n\n```rust\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_slices.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n        mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Update mat_slices with computed offsets\nfor (s, &o) in mat_slices.iter_mut().zip(&mat_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_slices.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n        sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\nfor (s, &o) in sel_slices.iter_mut().zip(&sel_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors (reclaim GPU memory)\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: The initial D2D pack costs ~2-3ms but enables uniform code for all rounds (no round-1 special case). The ~2-3ms is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding, netting 10-17ms improvement."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2922,"cache_read_input_tokens":274221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2922},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f518d6-4de0-4c05-9b5a-ade72ff81f39","uuid":"235de4f9-28a3-4211-8fda-7cf7c9d30be2"}
